<article class="env-lemma" id="05TS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05TS">Lemma <span data-tag="05TS">13.26.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with enough injectives. For any object $A$ of $\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})$ there exists a strict monomorphism $A \to I$ where $I$ is a filtered injective object. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Pick $a \leq b$ such that $\text{gr}^ p(A) = 0$ unless $p \in \{ a, a + 1, \ldots , b\} $. For each $n \in \{ a, a + 1, \ldots , b\} $ choose an injection $u_ n : A/F^{n + 1}A \to I_ n$ with $I_ n$ an injective object. Set $I = \bigoplus _{a \leq n \leq b} I_ n$ with filtration $F^ pI = \bigoplus _{n \geq p} I_ n$ and set $u : A \to I$ equal to the direct sum of the maps $u_ n$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>